hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15625","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Ghasil narrated to us, he said: Hamzah ibn Abi Usayd informed us, and his father was a participant at Badr, from al-Harith ibn Ziyad al-Saidi al-Ansari, that he came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the day of the Trench while he was pledging the people to emigration, and said: O Messenger of Allah, pledge this. He said: Who is this. He said: My cousin Hawt ibn Yazid, or Yazid ibn Hawt. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I will not pledge you. People emigrate to you and you do not emigrate to them. By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, no man loves the Ansar until he meets Allah, Blessed and Exalted, except he meets Allah, Blessed and Exalted, while He loves him, and no man hates the Ansar until he meets Allah, Blessed and Exalted, except he meets Allah, Blessed and Exalted, while He hates him."
"15626","Waki said: Sad ibn Aws narrated to me, from Bilal ibn Yahya, a shaykh of theirs, from Shutayr ibn Shakl, from his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me a supplication I may benefit by. He said: Say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of my hearing and my sight and my heart and my semen."
"15627","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sad ibn Aws narrated to us, from Bilal al-Absi, from Shutayr ibn Shakl, from his father Shakl ibn Humayd, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then he mentioned the hadith."
